{"agent_id":"pp3g-gUUV-third-verification-issue-404-independently-verify-the","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-08-18T15:37:59.549461458Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"423a26ad-8367-4629-9bd7-18744aacd9b5","comment_uuid":"3d144b36-9004-4b5f-a587-d7cf29e5e69d","author":"pp3g-gUUV-third-verification-issue-404-independently-verify-the","content":"## AUDIT VERDICT: CONDITIONAL PASS\n\n**Agent:** pp3g-gUUV-third-verification-issue-404-independently-verify-the\n**Audit scope:** Independently verify the hook-inventory deliverable from #391 -- hookability classifications per playbook section, mechanism assignments, already-hook-enforced claims, and priority ranking.\n\n---\n\n### Verification Performed\n\nIndependently read and verified all 8 infrastructure files against the inventory claims:\n\n| File | Read | Verified |\n|------|------|----------|\n| .opencode/plugins/crosslink-guard.ts | 1220 lines | Yes |\n| .opencode/plugins/orchestrator-guard.ts | 108 lines | Yes |\n| .opencode/plugins/rtk-guard.ts | 415 lines | Yes |\n| .crosslink/hook-config.json | 237 lines | Yes |\n| .opencode/opencode.json | 46 lines | Yes |\n| .opencode/permissions.md | 151 lines | Yes |\n| tools/kickoff-notify.py | 455 lines | Yes |\n| .claude/hooks/heartbeat.py | 86 lines | Yes |\n| .claude/hooks/crosslink_config.py | 363 lines | Yes |\n| .crosslink/knowledge/agent-orchestration-playbook.md | ~850 lines grep-verified | Yes |\n\n---\n\n### FINDING 1: Factual Inaccuracy -- Script Count\n\nThe inventory existing-hook-infrastructure table lists \"5 scripts\" (2 Claude Code hooks + 3 OpenCode plugins). This is misleading: heartbeat.py and crosslink_config.py are Claude Code PreToolUse/PostToolUse hooks in .claude/hooks/, while the .ts files are OpenCode plugins in .opencode/plugins/. They run in different runtimes and are loaded by different systems. The table conflates them into one list without distinguishing the loading mechanism. **Severity: LOW -- cosmetic.**\n\n---\n\n### FINDING 2: Misattribution -- Orchestrator Write Block\n\nThe inventory claims \"ALREADY ENFORCED by orchestrator-guard.ts + crosslink-guard.ts narrow bash allowlist\" for section 1.1 (orchestrator never implements). This is partially wrong:\n\n- **orchestrator-guard.ts** blocks write/edit/apply_patch/filesystem_write_file/filesystem_edit_file for non-Builder agents at tool.execute.before -- this IS the enforcement mechanism.\n- **crosslink-guard.ts** does NOT enforce orchestrator write blocking. It enforces git command gating and active-issue enforcement.\n- The \"narrow bash allowlist\" for the orchestrator comes from hook-config.json agent_overrides.by_type.orchestrator, not from crosslink-guard.ts itself.\n\n**Severity: MEDIUM -- misattributes the enforcement mechanism. The claim that orchestrator-guard.ts enforces this is correct; adding crosslink-guard.ts as a co-enforcer is wrong.**\n\n---\n\n### FINDING 3: Inaccurate Enforcer Attribution -- Section 1.3 Workers\n\nThe inventory claims section 1.3 (workers never plan/review/merge to master) is \"ALREADY ENFORCED: task deny + git push/merge blocked\". This is partially accurate but imprecise:\n\n- \"task deny\" refers to the permissions.md task permission setting -- this is a permission-model constraint, not a hook enforcement. The inventory conflates permission-based enforcement with hook-based enforcement.\n- \"git push/merge blocked\" -- git push IS blocked for all agents by crosslink-guard.ts. Git merge is blocked for non-orchestrator agents via hook-config.json by_type.blocked_git_commands. For orchestrators, merge is gated (requires active issue), not blocked.\n\n**Severity: MEDIUM -- conflates permission-model enforcement with hook enforcement.**\n\n---\n\n### FINDING 4: Correct -- Section 9.3 Orchestrator Merge Gated\n\nThe inventory correctly identifies that section 9.3 (orchestrator merge gated on active issue) is enforced. Verified: hook-config.json by_type.orchestrator.gated_git_commands includes \"git merge\". crosslink-guard.ts enforces the active-issue gate on gated commands. **CONFIRMED.**\n\n---\n\n### FINDING 5: Correct -- Section 6.4 Lifecycle Watcher\n\nThe inventory correctly identifies the lifecycle watcher as \"ALREADY IMPLEMENTED\" via kickoff-notify.py + systemd timer. Verified: kickoff-notify.py implements LAUNCHING to RUNNING to DONE or FAILED or CI_FAILED state machine, STALLED detection via heartbeat staleness, notify-send + webhook notifications. **CONFIRMED.**\n\n---\n\n### FINDING 6: HIGH-PRIORITY Gaps Correctly Identified\n\nThe inventory correctly identifies these as NOT ENFORCED:\n\n| Claim | Verified Status |\n|-------|----------------|\n| Section 3.1 --model required on kickoff/swarm | NOT ENFORCED -- no validation in any guard plugin or shell wrapper |\n| Section 5.3.1 Reject blanket 1h timeout | NOT ENFORCED -- no timeout validation in any guard plugin |\n| Section 6.3.3 Empty review output triggers CRASH | NOT ENFORCED -- no review-length check in any guard plugin |\n| Section 12.1 Session end requires --notes | NOT ENFORCED -- no --notes check in any guard plugin |\n\n**CONFIRMED: these are genuine hookable gaps.**\n\n---\n\n### FINDING 7: Inventory Overstates Enforcement Breadth\n\nThe inventory summary claims \"~15 rules are ALREADY hook-enforced today\". After verification, I count **~10 rules with direct hook/plugin enforcement**:\n\n1. Orchestrator write blocking -- orchestrator-guard.ts\n2. Git push blocked for all agents -- crosslink-guard.ts\n3. Git merge blocked for non-orchestrator agents -- crosslink-guard.ts + hook-config.json\n4. Git merge gated on active issue for orchestrator -- crosslink-guard.ts + hook-config.json\n5. Git commit gated on active issue -- crosslink-guard.ts + hook-config.json\n6. Comment discipline -- plan comment required -- crosslink-guard.ts\n7. Comment discipline -- result comment required before close -- crosslink-guard.ts\n8. Active-issue enforcement for write/edit/bash -- crosslink-guard.ts\n9. Kill/pause flags -- crosslink-guard.ts\n10. RTK command rewriting -- rtk-guard.ts\n\nPlus 2 infrastructure hooks:\n11. Heartbeats -- heartbeat.py\n12. Lifecycle watcher -- kickoff-notify.py\n\nThe remaining \"~15\" count in the inventory includes rules where enforcement is via the permission model (permissions.md) rather than hooks, which is a different enforcement mechanism. **Severity: MEDIUM -- inflates the hook-enforcement surface.**\n\n---\n\n### FINDING 8: Hookability Classifications -- Spot-Checked\n\nThe inventory hookability classifications for \"NOT hookable\" rules are semantically sound. Spot-checked:\n\n- Section 1.2 Orchestrator never reviews own work -- requires semantic judgment -- correctly classified NOT hookable\n- Section 2.1-2.3 Tier selection -- requires complexity assessment -- correctly classified NOT hookable\n- Section 5.5 Two-repo sync -- requires cross-repo coordination -- correctly classified NOT hookable\n- Section 7.1-7.4 Failure protocol -- requires intent detection -- correctly classified NOT hookable\n\n**CONFIRMED: hookability classifications are reasonable.**\n\n---\n\n### FINDING 9: Mechanism Legend Correct\n\nThe inventory mechanism legend (a through e) is accurate:\n- (a) OpenCode plugin tool.execute.before/after\n- (b) Claude Code PreToolUse/PostToolUse\n- (c) crosslink CLI hookpoint\n- (d) shell wrapper\n- (e) NOT hookable\n\n**CONFIRMED.**\n\n---\n\n### FINDING 10: Priority Ranking Sound\n\nThe HIGH-PRIORITY gap items (--model enforcement, timeout validation, empty review, session end --notes) are correctly prioritized by failure frequency and implementation cost. These are the most impactful hooks that could be built with trivial code additions. **CONFIRMED.**\n\n---\n\n### WHAT-NOT-TESTED\n\n1. **Playbook section completeness**: I did not read every line of the 825-line playbook to verify every single rule classification. I spot-checked the claims that were verifiable against the infrastructure files. A complete section-by-section audit would require reading the full playbook and cross-referencing each row.\n2. **Runtime behavior**: I verified the code structure and logic, but did not run the plugins in a live OpenCode session to confirm they fire as expected.\n3. **crosslink CLI fork changes**: The inventory mentions crosslink CLI hookpoints (mechanism c) -- I did not verify whether the crosslink CLI actually exposes these hookpoints.\n\n---\n\n### VERDICT: CONDITIONAL PASS\n\nThe inventory is substantively correct on its core claims:\n- The existing hook infrastructure is accurately described (with FINDING 2 and 3 as caveats on enforcement attribution)\n- The HIGH-PRIORITY hookable gaps are correctly identified and verified as not enforced\n- The hookability classifications are semantically sound\n- The priority ranking is reasonable\n\n**Conditions for full PASS:**\n1. Correct the \"5 scripts\" count to distinguish OpenCode plugins from Claude Code hooks (FINDING 1)\n2. Remove crosslink-guard.ts as a co-enforcer for section 1.1 orchestrator write blocking -- orchestrator-guard.ts is the sole enforcer (FINDING 2)\n3. Distinguish permission-model enforcement from hook enforcement in the \"ALREADY ENFORCED\" claims (FINDING 3)\n4. Revise \"~15 rules ALREADY hook-enforced\" to \"~12 rules with hook/plugin enforcement\" (FINDING 7)\n\nThese are factual corrections, not structural flaws. The inventory value as a hookability audit is intact.","created_at":"2026-08-18T15:37:59.540886919Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:jWuaMyIulS/1so0HHrcpCBbTgJ+p63M2Vvlxb2Znbok","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgmv9TN0F2bsLnBA5khaToHPOF3hHwY/9reM5OpcUOoVAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAapYIc3NYzVr47/4nZJCOt9r7avDZ8dkdSCWwuzzbWruCaUtaPAAL8sJbSc8/6ANoPw9HXDZAEi+4RAG9EV2bBQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:jWuaMyIulS/1so0HHrcpCBbTgJ+p63M2Vvlxb2Znbok","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgmv9TN0F2bsLnBA5khaToHPOF3hHwY/9reM5OpcUOoVAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMODlnyozLGP1+NvXjFE+W3BcCDfvVwe+yE1a6pOTQGDzvDzyJt2rpiBOPZ91StuNSKwEoCifFela+mk7se+aAM="}
